# Generated by `node tools/polestar.js profession gathering build` from tools/lib/professions/routes/herbalism.json and data/forever. Do not edit: rebuild with that command.
guide forever/professions/herbalism
title Herbalism 1-300
category Professions
coords era
levels 1-60
zone Azeroth

# Herbalism picks herbs from the plants that grow across the world. Alchemy brews them into potions
# and elixirs, so the two go well together. It needs no tool.
#
# Ranks: Apprentice at any level; Journeyman from skill 50, Expert from 125 and Artisan from 200, at
# the trainers in every capital and the larger towns. The trainers in the starting areas teach only up
# to 75. Tanaris and Searing Gorge have no trainer, so Artisan comes before the trip there. On Zephras
# Isle the quest Harvesting Windstones offers Wild Harvest, which teaches Herbalism.
#
# Optional skill bonuses: Enchant Gloves - Herbalism (+2) or Advanced Herbalism (+5), Herbalist's
# Gloves (+5, a world drop), Apothecary Gloves (+2, from the Horde quest Serpentbloom in Thunder
# Bluff) and Goldthorn Tea (+15 for a while; its recipe comes from Henry Stern in Razorfen Downs and
# needs Cooking 175). With +5, Kingsblood can be picked from 120.
#
# Each gathering step offers areas to roam with the most of what the skill can gather (the server's
# own spawns, how often each is up, and what players' recorded gathers gave): the window lists those
# for your level, best first, the arrow leads to the one you pick and rests once you are in it, never
# among creatures two or more levels above you, and away from the other faction's towns and guards.
# Waypoints are Era-frame; a map without one (Zephras Isle) compiles live.

section Herbalism 1-70

step Learn Herbalism
  tip No character level needed. On Zephras Isle, Wild Harvest from Harvesting Windstones teaches it too.
  train Herbalism Apprentice

step Turn on Find Herbs · Professions tab (K by default)
  tip Herbs show on the minimap. Dying turns it off, and only one kind of tracking is on at a time.
  cast 2383 "Find Herbs"

step Pick Peacebloom and Silverleaf until 15
  tip Herbs grow everywhere in the starting areas and come back fast.
